.nh
.TH "PB-RECIPE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recipe - Create and manage recipes that pair and set up machines


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recipe [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
A recipe is a small JSON file (with comments, .jsonc) that says what happens on a machine when it
joins: its tags, what it may reach, which ENV vaults it reads, which repository it
pulls config from, which preview or tunnel it opens, and when it is removed. Create
one with pb recipe create -f ci.jsonc; the printed token, set as PB_RECIPE, pairs and
sets up a machine with one command and no prompt.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for recipe


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-create(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-revoke(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-rotate(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-schema(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-show(1)\fP, \fBpb-recipe-update(1)\fP
